Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.418
Mars.

00:00:01.418 --> 00:00:04.254
I always
wonder what it would be like to live there

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.588
And to build there.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:19.644
What would it feel like to look out the window
and see an alien landscape

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:23.898
millions and millions of miles away
from everything we know.

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:26.526
Although the exact timeline is unclear.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.486
We're definitely planning

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:32.365
for a new life on Mars
and we're putting a lot of money into it.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:36.619
NASA has plans to send their first human
missions sometime in 2030,

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:42.792
SpaceX by 2029, and also establish
a city of 1 million by 2050.

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:47.756
The Emirates plans to build
a human settlement by the year 2117,

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:51.593
although there are still a lot
of variables and unknowns

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:55.764
in the last couple of years,
we found potential water , they found

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:58.725
Organic molecules hinting to signs of life

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.771
and technology is accelerating
at an insane rate.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:06.066
This video
sponsored and brainstormed with Milanote

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.401
More on them later in this video.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:16.534
The Kardashev scale is a method of
assessing the technological capabilities

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.871
of a civilization
based on the amount of energy it can use

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:22.624
and manipulate.

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:28.296
A Type one civilization has full control
over all of our energy sources.

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:31.257
We're currently at type 0.72,

00:01:31.341 --> 00:01:34.177
but we are on track to reaching type one.

00:01:34.302 --> 00:01:37.013
And once we get there,
according to Kardashev,

00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:41.226
we're going to have such a profound
understanding of science and technology.

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:45.605
We're going to be able to manipulate
matter and energy on a molecular level.

00:01:45.897 --> 00:01:48.316
We're going to have control over the water
patterns,

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:51.778
and we're even going to be able
to colonize other planets.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:55.323
So maybe it's just a matter of time

00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:58.201
that humans start to expand
beyond our planet.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:01.412
But what kind of conditions do
we need to build for humans

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:04.457
to really live there and not just survive?

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.961
And is our species even ready for this?

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:15.718
Right now, the focus
for the next couple of decades is getting

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:19.848
the first few astronauts to live there
for an extended period of time.

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:23.017
But I think
once that mission is successful, it's

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:27.313
really a matter of time
until we get the first pioneers

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:31.025
who are the selected test group who's
going to continue to do research on Mars,

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:35.655
and the first settlers, the first Mars
community to permanently live there.

00:02:35.947 --> 00:02:40.326
And one day
we will have a human colony on Mars.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:44.622
They'll probably think and maybe
even look very different from us.

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:48.126
Each of these categories of people
are going to have a very different

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:52.589
experience of Mars depending
on the technical apparatus of that time.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.718
And we're still quite a ways away
from being able to modify the Martian

00:02:56.718 --> 00:03:01.723
atmosphere and be able to experience Mars
as we currently live on Earth.

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:03.933
Right now, we're in this very first stage.

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:07.187
But this is a really critical point

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:12.025
because once we get past this mark,
where we're not just surviving

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:17.071
but thriving on Mars, it's going
to open the doors to a whole new frontier

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:21.075
and becoming a multi-planet species
where we could feel confident

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:25.622
about creating
new habitats wherever we go.

00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:33.129
There
have been lots of different proposals

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:37.300
for habitation on Mars,
but it seems like we are leaning

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.429
towards a construction method
that's a combination of prefabrication

00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:45.016
and 3D printing
using the local material on Mars.

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:48.186
So in 2019, NASA held a competition

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:51.022
to design a 3D printed habitat on Mars

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:54.275
to house four astronauts
for the time span of a year.

00:03:54.484 --> 00:03:57.654
They were given a set
of functional requirements like a lab,

00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:01.366
a kitchen, a rec room, and 1000
square feet of living space,

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:06.120
all designed for the astronauts
to conduct research while living there.

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:08.915
If these habitats prove to be successful,

00:04:09.207 --> 00:04:13.211
these modules should be easily replicable
for further expansion.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.880
Each of these proposals
use a phased strategy

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.926
where they send autonomous machines
to first harvest

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:23.137
the raw Martian materials,
and then they create a building

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:26.975
material using the Martian soil
and other composites.

00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:30.311
And then they 3D print
the initial framework

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:33.398
for the habitat
before the astronauts actually get there.

00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:37.610
Once this is built,
the outfit, the interior, either

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.156
through an inflatable structure
or any other prefabricated components

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:45.994
that come together
on the inside of the shell.

